  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the person as the recipient of angelic reward for not stealing",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'person' (the woman in the angelic scene) because the text 'when you haven't stolen anything in a week' uses the second-person pronoun 'you', directly addressing the viewer. The user identifies with the 'you' in the text, imagining themselves as the person who has abstained from theft and thus is deserving of the angelic reward depicted. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'person', who is symbolically the recipient of the reward described in the text.",
